course: dictionary
lesson: 13589
title: Incompetence: when the skill is missing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Incompetence is a noun. It means you lack the skill or ability to do a job properly, so you do it badly because you do not know how. Look at the parts of the word: «competent» means able and skilful, and the prefix in- means not. So incompetence is the state of not being competent.
explain: Read the words around it to find the clues. «The plumber's incompetence flooded the kitchen.» The flood is the bad result, so the plumber did the job badly. Ask yourself: what went wrong, and why? Incompetence often explains the answer.
explain: Stories use this word a lot. «The villain's incompetence let the hero escape.» The villain was not clever or skilled enough to stop the hero, so the hero got away. Look for the phrases «sheer incompetence» (pure lack of skill), «through incompetence» (because of a lack of skill) and «gross incompetence» (very serious, a formal phrase).
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. Try «The plumber's lack of skill flooded the kitchen.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Incompetence means lack of the skill or ability needed to do a job properly.
fact: It comes from «competent», which means able and skilful at something.
fact: The prefix in- means not, so incompetent means not competent.
fact: «Sheer incompetence» means complete lack of skill, and «gross incompetence» is a formal way to say it is very serious.
fact: Adults can lose their jobs because of incompetence, when they cannot do the work properly.
exercise: «The rescue team's incompetence meant the boat sank.» What does incompetence mean? | Being too tired to work | Working too fast | Being very brave in danger | *Lack of the skill needed to do the job properly
exercise: In incompetence, the in- at the start means what? | *Not | Before | Again | Very
exercise: «The mess was caused by sheer incompetence.» Find and copy the phrase that means complete lack of skill. | the mess | was caused | by sheer | *sheer incompetence
test: «The shop closed through incompetence, not bad luck.» Why did the shop close? | *Because the owners lacked the skill to run it well | Because the shop was too popular | Because it was a holiday | Because of a storm
test: Which word is the opposite of incompetence? | Confusion | *Competence | Laziness | Carelessness
exam: A report says the mess was «gross incompetence». What is the writer saying? | The mess was small and easy to fix | The mess was made on purpose by a clever plan | *The mess was caused by a very serious lack of skill | The mess was a fun surprise
